His tone was fierce yet gentle, and he pulled me out of the scene, in front of the elevator. He was still holding onto my arms, without saying anything. I could hear the sound of the elevator coming up.

[current layer="message0"]
[layopt layer="message1" visible=false]
[layopt layer="message0" visible=true]
[image storage=default/UI_Elements/stellar_ui_chat2big.png layer=1 x=35 y=458 visible=true time=0 width=181 height=217]
[chara_mod name="Alexei" storage="/chara/4/alex_lookout.png" time=200 cross=false]
...[l]Are you alright? [p]
[freeimage layer=1]
[current layer="message1"]
[layopt layer="message0" visible=false]
[layopt layer="message1" visible=true]

I wasn't, of course. [l]But I couldn't answer him that. [l]I couldn't just straight up tell him I wanted to die myself, after witnessing something like that. [p]
[playse storage=SoundEffects_Action/door1_soft.ogg loop=false clear=false layer=1]
[chara_show  name="Klaus"  time="1000"  wait="false"  storage="chara/2/klaus_angry.png"  width="495"  height="720"  left="150"  top="0"  reflect="false"]
[chara_show  name="Joshua"  time="1000"  wait="true"  storage="chara/3/joshua_angry.png"  width="495"  height="720"  left="730"  top="0"  reflect="false"]
The only working elevator opens, with Klaus and Joshua barging out of it. [l]
[chara_mod name="Klaus" storage="/chara/3/joshua_surprised.png" time=200 cross=false]
[chara_hide  name="Klaus"  time="1000"  wait="false"  pos_mode="true"]
Joshua came to me, while Klaus went towards Nicola's corpse without blinking at me. [l]
[chara_show  name="Klaus"  time="1000"  wait="false"  storage="chara/2/klaus_wary_normal.png"  width="495"  height="720"  left="150"  top="0"  reflect="false"]
And for the very first time, I saw Klaus flinch. [p]
Joshua rushed to see Nicola as well, but quickly turned his head, leaning on the the wall before sitting down suddenly, holding his head in grief. [l]You would expect him of all people to scream or shout at someone, but instead, like Klaus, his behavior while facing such a gruesome scene turned his usual behavior upside down. [p]

[fadeoutbgm time=3000]
...The room was completely silenced. The sound of the meteorites completely stopped a while ago now, and after such a twisted turn of events, everyone decided to stay in silence, instead of asking questions.
Usually, Nicola was the one to break the silence. And in this dreadful shock we were all in, it's like we expected Nicola to rise up and tell us to cheer up. This, of course, will never happen.
Klaus, as expected, was the one to break up the silence. He approached Nicola's body. After gaining some composure, I slowly decide to follow him, courage in hand. I need to face this situation, no matter what. If I don't do it now, no one will do it for me. Alexeï watched us from afar with a suspicious eye, while Joshua was still sitting nearby, gazing at nothing.
"Don't disrupt the scene."
Unexpectedly, Alexeï spoke up.
"I will not."
Klaus was analyzing her body. I too, chose to be brave and look at her corpse in more detail. I don't know how I didn't realize it sooner, but part of her coat was ripped.
"...Her body is in a clean state, except for this cut on her throat. She's definitely been killed.
-...How can you be so sure?
-How can I be so sure...? Are you serious? Are you implying this was a suicide?
-We can't eliminate this possibility.
-We can.
-What the hell?
-If this was a suicide, this scene wouldn't be such a mess. Even her coat is ripped, and we've yet to see the missing piece.
-...Are you implying one of us did it, then? Be careful with what you say. By accusing one of us, you're putting all of us in great danger.
-But everyone was busy, and out from the observatory! Do I also have to remind you that there was only one working elevator?"
Joshua jumped up to say this.
"This is something we'll have to clear up. Until we receive external help, we have no way of knowing more about her death until we all gather around and discuss this properly, before doubting each other."
Klaus opened the elevator, and went in without us moving an inch.
"I'll be right back. I'm going to get a sheet to cover her body. I'm sure she wouldn't have wanted us to see her like that."
Nobody answered back, and he went down without adding anything more. I was still looking at Nicola's body. I needed to know as much as I could, to uncover the truth. There were a bunch of papers everywhere, both on the desk and the floor. Some with formulas, and some others with information about meteorites. There were a few writing tools scattered around, but a specific pen was brought to my attention. It was drenched with blood unto the very top, but it didn't seem like it came from the puddle of blood. There also seemed to be slight bits of... Skin on it. But the only bloody part of her body was her neck, and there's no way this pen could have been used as the murder weapon. Her palms weren't bleeding, either. The only blood we could see was the now dry substance coming out of her neck. That probably meant...
"Euphémia, please move."
Klaus was already back. I didn't even hear him coming back.
"Sorry."
Klaus gently placed the sheet on her corpse. It was like doing a final farewell. Instead of crying, I decided to stop my tears flowing through sheer determination. I will uncover what happened here, no matter the cost. And I will not let anyone stain my dream with unnecessary death.
"Whoever is responsible will pay, and I'll make sure order stays in this group."
Those words came out of my mind, and the three remaining members were understandably surprised. After saying that, I needed to keep their attention.
"For now, I think we all need to settle down, and figure something out to get out of this situation in the best way. ...And get something to eat to get our blood flowing again."
Though I'm not hungry myself.
They all quietly nodded, and we all took some dry and cold food to gather in the lounge, that I've still yet to see for myself.

